262	FACTS.md:27
263	- **Walk's load check reads a generic declaration beside a plain one on declared domains, and covers an overlap through `comprises` clauses, where its parameter-by-parameter check refuses** (`compile-ladder/rung-walk-dispatch/REPORT.md` sections 5.3 and 5.4; POSITIONS, "Conversions never change which declaration runs" and "The `comprises` passages read at the level of values (PLAN item 26, row 491)"; row 492, fixed). Both run only where the parameter-by-parameter check refuses (`OverloadedFunction.java:497-500`). For one own generic beside a plain declaration, `validOnDeclaredDomains` (`:693-722`) compares declared domains under the return-type rule and accepts an overlap that plain declarations below both cover, reading each parameter of the generic as the types whose intersection holds its values: a type parameter as its bounds that name no static parameter, a type that mentions a static parameter as `Any`, a non-type static parameter as no reason to refuse (`genericOverlapCovered`, `:728-778`; `intersectionPieces`, `:917-976`; row 552, fixed); for two plain declarations with an unrelated parameter pair, `overlapCovered` (`:814-825`; `overlapPieces`, `:986-1030`) cuts the overlap by the `comprises` clauses and needs every part inside one declaration below both, refusing what it cannot settle. Two generic declarations take the parameter-by-parameter check alone (Q4 = (1)). Gated by `tests/ComprisesMeetWalk.fss`, `ComprisesCoverReturn.fss`, `GenericBesidePlainTwoBounds.fss` and `GenericBesidePlainOverlapShapes.fss` (row 552), and the refusals `XXXGenericBesidePlainReturnRule.fss`, `XXXComprisesMeetUncovered`, `XXXComprisesCoverReturnWrong` and `XXXOverloadExistentialMeetWalk.fss` (row 539). Walk checks the closure of the main component's `comprises` clauses (row 551), not yet the library's (rows 595, 596), another component's (row 551) or an object expression's (row 597; "Walk checks at load the `comprises` clauses of the program's main component ..." below).
264	
265	FACTS.md:29
266	- **Walk checks at load the `comprises` clauses of the program's main component, and its harness names an expected refusal at load** (`compile-ladder/rung-walk-load-check/REPORT.md`; row 552 fixed, row 551 for the main component's clauses). `BuildEnvironments.checkComprisesClauses`, called from `Driver.evalComponent` once every component's types are built, reads the declarations as written and asks every extender of a closed trait of the main component for the traits chapter's three eligible forms, reading a generic child's extenders across the whole program; the library's clauses (rows 595, 596), another component's (row 551), an object expression (row 597) and the clause's other half, that a listed type extends each instantiation (row 598), are not read. A file `Name.fss` of `tests/` names its refusal in `Name.test` by `load_exception_contains` (`FileTests.java`, `InterpreterTest.loadRefusalKeys`): a plain test passes when walk refuses the program at load as named, an `XXX` test when the program loads and runs clean; a failure while the top-level variables are initialized counts as a refusal at load. Gated by `tests/ComprisesUnlistedExtender`, `ComprisesGenericChildUnlistedExtender`, `GenericBesidePlainOverlapShapes` and the `XXX` files of rows 22, 487, 534, 544, 549, 597 and 598.
