275	FACTS.md:137
276	- **Under `walk`, a type parameter that nothing at a call fixes takes its declared bound, and a lone one with no narrowest candidate its bound** (`compile-ladder/rung-walk-instance/REPORT.md` section 2, its decisions D2, D3 and D5 in `decision-record.md`; rows 424, 516, 555, 558, 567). Where walk instantiates the declaration a call runs (`EvaluatorBase.inferAndInstantiateGenericFunction`, the instance `instanceOf`, `interpreter/evaluator/EvaluatorBase.java:156-188`) the bound is `Any` if none is written, and a join of several minimal common supertypes takes the bound too; a typecase that matches nothing throws `MatchFailure`, which the one library declares checked (row 590), and generic functional methods run (`GenericFunctionalMethod.Own`). Left at `BottomType`: an F-bounded parameter, a big operator's static parameters (D2), a parameter declared with several bounds walk cannot meet (row 591), one that an argument bounds only from above (row 588) and one that only an untyped function expression's result fixes (row 587). A parameter that only another fixed parameter's bound mentions takes the arguments' type (row 592, D3), and a lone parameter whose bound mentions a static parameter keeps the arguments' narrowest named common supertype (D5). Where walk chooses among declarations the lattice's join decides, so a generic whose arguments have several minimal common supertypes gives way to any declaration applicable without coercion (row 589), and where none applies walk's coercion pass finds it applicable at its bound (`InferTwoCommonParentsWalk.fss`, `either`). Gated by `tests/InferUnfixedBoundWalk.fss`, `InferLoneUnboundedWalk.fss`, `InferTwoCommonParentsWalk.fss`, `TypecaseNoMatchWalk.fss`, `GenericFunctionalMethodWalk.fss` and `GenericTraitGenericFunctionalMethodWalk.fss`, the departures by `XXXInferSeveralBoundsWalk.fss`, `XXXInferContravariantWalk.fss`, `XXXInferThroughBoundWalk.fss` and `XXXInferUntypedLambdaResultWalk.fss`.
