289	- **`testSystem`'s four shards are one suite split by sorted index, so per-shard counts are not comparable across a change to the interpreter corpus and only their sum is** (`compile-ladder/climb-batch-2/JUDGE-gate.md`). `FileTests.java:907-923` sorts the files of `tests/` and keeps index `j` when `j % 4 == i` (root `build.xml:1171-1211`, the `systemShard` macro), so a file added moves every later entry along the shards (`compile-ladder/climb-batch-2/repair/shard-membership.sh`). `gate_compare` (the gate's step 5, in `gateRole` of `coordinator/climb-batch-workflow.js`) sums the `system-<i>` rows before comparing.
